[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-GLOSSES-INTERIM
TITLE: The grammar tab's glosses are a hand copy of the canon narrative
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The Grammars tab's axis and type glosses are hard-coded in
docs/sdoc/board/grammar-groups.json, copied verbatim out of two different
canon sources: the four axis glosses out of NAR-CANON-TYPES-GRID, and each
type gloss out of the first sentence of that type's NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-*
narrative. Two copies of the same words drift, and only the coverage check
(dev/scripts/grammar-groups-check.py) notices a missing type, not a stale
gloss. The fix is blocked on the option-1-versus-2 call about where glosses
live; cheapest interim guard is a check that each copied sentence still
matches its own source -- which means reading two kinds of file, not one.
<<<
